    {
      "id": "HMUoP4MRK689CXA-Y57yT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 811.1123806718754,
      "y": 1593.590639,
      "width": 339.61572265625,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1189053926,
      "version": 997,
      "versionNonce": 853778298,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795537272021,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A(2,1) is loaded by thread (2,3),\nwhich owns no spot in C. \n\nBut thread (2,2) in C needs the value that\nthread (2,3) loaded, which is A(2,1).\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A(2,1) is loaded by thread (2,3),\nwhich owns no spot in C. \n\nBut thread (2,2) in C needs the value that\nthread (2,3) loaded, which is A(2,1).\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vU8dpu2GJ3H0OVUdPMNMS",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 746,
      "y": 1602,
      "width": 61,
      "height": 51,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#6741d9",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1614232486,
      "version": 63,
      "versionNonce": 1627713658,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795535958563,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2idkrruN2Hb0aNYG-nrn8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 450.7444293593751,
      "y": 1762.892733,
      "width": 660.04736328125,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 722112678,
      "version": 1520,
      "versionNonce": 889178214,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795537406214,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A thread outside of C can't just stop early. It still has a loading job: \nit fills its slot of each tile, because other threads in the block may need that value.\n\nIt must also reach every barrier, like the others, or the rest of block would wait\nat the barrier forever.\n\nThe only thing it skips is the write to C, since its spot of C doesn't exist.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A thread outside of C can't just stop early. It still has a loading job: \nit fills its slot of each tile, because other threads in the block may need that value.\n\nIt must also reach every barrier, like the others, or the rest of block would wait\nat the barrier forever.\n\nThe only thing it skips is the write to C, since its spot of C doesn't exist.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "efwVwMbab-AxM5M8GgqRH",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 436.2994350000001,
      "y": 1921.8624548888888,
      "width": 715.4777479999998,
      "height": 477.77777733333306,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1999687418,
      "version": 156,
      "versionNonce": 654963450,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795537398723,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qefY46ph1MtMqgoDFZwlm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 752.4611166590713,
      "y": 1922.9735664444443,
      "width": 71.29998779296875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 712568230,
      "version": 587,
      "versionNonce": 1980072890,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795537398723,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTES",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTES",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "m3WKWlNMYQ_mGq6QGmWYj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 464.3013576931426,
      "y": 1960.586018777777,
      "width": 647.6195068359375,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1802568890,
      "version": 1222,
      "versionNonce": 684784762,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795537398723,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When the width is not a multiple of the tile width,\nthe last blocks and tiles stick out past the edge of the matrices.\n\nReading outside is never safe: past the end of the row you \nget the next row's value, past the end of the array garbage or\ncrash.\n\nEvery memory access gets its own check.\n\n0 adds nothing to the dot product, so the padded slots are\nharmless.\n\nA thread outside C still loads and still reaches every barrier:\nits value may be needed by others, and every thread must arrive.\n\nRule of thumb: check every global read and write,\nbut never skip a barrier.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When the width is not a multiple of the tile width,\nthe last blocks and tiles stick out past the edge of the matrices.\n\nReading outside is never safe: past the end of the row you \nget the next row's value, past the end of the array garbage or\ncrash.\n\nEvery memory access gets its own check.\n\n0 adds nothing to the dot product, so the padded slots are\nharmless.\n\nA thread outside C still loads and still reaches every barrier:\nits value may be needed by others, and every thread must arrive.\n\nRule of thumb: check every global read and write,\nbut never skip a barrier.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TiFV3TxQ4LyjGHnsBhVBL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1170.0090823703342,
      "y": 1547.4722222222224,
      "width": 441.7596130371094,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 6458362,
      "version": 1271,
      "versionNonce": 1957760294,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795537557496,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Threads outside of C have loading jobs that\nother threads rely on, so they must keep going\nthrough every phase and barrier, and only skip the write.\n\nEvery thread in the block loads one value of A and one\nvalue of B each phase, and a value can be a real one\nor 0, depending on whether its spot is inside of A or B.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Threads outside of C have loading jobs that\nother threads rely on, so they must keep going\nthrough every phase and barrier, and only skip the write.\n\nEvery thread in the block loads one value of A and one\nvalue of B each phase, and a value can be a real one\nor 0, depending on whether its spot is inside of A or B.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
